# LOCKED: 3D dental viewer

The register-page 3D jaw viewer is **permanently locked**. Form fields, dropdowns, headers, footers, and layout tweaks must never change it.

## Do not modify these files

- `components/dental-jaw-3d.tsx`
- `components/dental-chart-scene.tsx`
- `components/interactive-dental-chart.tsx`
- `lib/dental-anatomy.ts`
- `lib/dental-chart.ts`
- `public/models/**`

Also leave the register 3D column untouched: the `h-[calc(100svh-8.5rem)] min-h-[32rem]` wrapper, `DentalJaw3D fill`, and the dark `/models` loading placeholder.

## Do not change

- Camera `{ position: [0, 0.22, 7.5], fov: 30 }`
- OrbitControls, lights/Environment intensity, gums, GLB teeth, flip/mirror/Spee/layout math
- Canvas transparency: WebGL `alpha: true`, clear alpha `0`, `scene.background = null`, no `<color attach="background">`, no ContactShadows floor, no local navy fill on the canvas. The static page background must show through. Do not restore an opaque `#01113a` scene/canvas background.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — editing the form is not a reason to touch the viewer
<Canvas camera={{ position: [0, 1, 5], fov: 45 }}>

// ✅ GOOD — change only form UI; keep DentalJaw3D as-is
<TreatmentTypeSelect className={fieldClassName} />
<div className="h-[calc(100svh-8.5rem)] min-h-[32rem] min-w-0">
  <DentalJaw3D fill selected={chartedTeeth} onChange={setChartedTeeth} />
</div>
```

If the canvas looks blank, fix WebGL **inside** `dental-jaw-3d.tsx` only (size, context restore, keep it transparent). Do not “fix” it by painting a local canvas color, editing the form, `SiteHeader`, or camera/model code.
